.TH POKER 6.SH NAMEpoker \- cold-hand poker against the computer.SH SYNOPSIS\fBpoker\fR.SH DESCRIPTIONFive-card poker.  It offers the rules, starts you with a stack of chips,asks the bet limit as a percentage of the pot and the ante, deals yourhand -- as rank and suit,\fB4S 7S 8H JH 6S\fR-- and asks whether you bet\fR(\fBB\fR)\fRor check\fR(\fB\-\fR).\fR.SH FILES.TP 12\fB/dd/GAMES/SNOBOL/PHRASE.SYN\fRthe phrases it talks in..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fROne of Robert Heller's programs translated from SNOBOL4 into C, fromJames F. Gimpel's\fIAlgorithms in SNOBOL4\fR;\fR\fBDOC/snobol\fRdescribes the set and\fBSRC/effo_snobol\fRholds the source..SH SEE ALSOblackjak